      "message": "So I think that Haneef is correct, we shouldn\u0027t be throwing a 401 for this specific problem.  What confuses this is that there are two situations:\n\n1) With domain specific backends when no domain is specified when listing users or groups.  I think this should throw a 403 (Forbidden).\n\n2) If you do specify a domain when listing users and groups, but you don\u0027t have a role that gives you access to that API, then we should (and do) throw a 401 (Unathorized).  This is irrespective of whether we are using domain specific backends or not.\n\nSo I think we should fix 1), along with this doc change, which would involve changing the exception thown at the end of _get_domain_id_for_list_request() in common/controller.py",
